# Restrict renv's dependency scan to the publication pipeline
# (simple_regression/) that renv.lock is meant to cover. Without this,
# renv scans the whole repo (2000+ files: archives, old phase_1/phase_2/
# phase3 exploration, election_data/Archive notebooks, the Python .venv,
# etc.), which is slow, pulls in packages no publication script uses
# (sf, MatchIt, tidyverse, RSelenium...), and even errors on a corrupted
# notebook under election_data/data_quentin/Archive/__MACOSX/.
#
# simple_regression/archives/ is excluded too -- superseded scripts, not
# part of the current pipeline (see simple_regression/publication/replication/README.md).
archives/
balancecompt/
data/
election_data/
make_parc_map.R
outputs/
phase_1/
phase_2/
phase3/
presentations/
scripts/
stats_des/
sumpowerdep.R
.venv/
simple_regression/archives/
